-- R46 - PLAIN READING AT THE TOP for both Takeaways (owner's ask 28 Nov 2026, thread "Drop question ids from 60-second
-- summary"; amended the same evening on his follow-up: no questions at all in the 60 seconds, no ids or arrows in READ
-- FIRST, question moves in words in the themes). In force 28 Nov by single-statement UPDATE; the amendment replaced
-- title and body the same way. "revert R46" removes it.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Plain reading at the top: no questions, ids or arrows in THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS or the READ FIRST box; question moves in plain words in each theme; tags and a table of every open question in OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD before the footer", "body": "PLAIN READING AT THE TOP, QUESTIONS IN THE THEMES AND AT THE END (owner's ask 28 Nov 2026, amended the same evening: the top of the edition must read fully to a friend who knows nothing of the question tracker; no question ids, no arrows, no tracker jargon there; question moves belong in plain words in the themes, and every open question's probability move in a table at the bottom).\n\n1. THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS is news only: what happened, with levels, times and sources. It prints no question at all: no \"Qnn\", no odds move of a tracked question, no \"[n · Qnn NET ...]\" label, no yellow question tag, no arrow (↑ ↓ ↔), no \"Priced:\", no \"[sweep]\" or \"[Δ ...]\" marker, no \"New question\" or \"resolved\" line. A market-implied probability may appear only as plain news (\"futures price a 94% chance of a 9 Dec Fed hike\"), never as a tracker move. Same items and facts as before otherwise.\n\n2. READ FIRST box: no question ids and no arrows anywhere in it (QUESTIONS and NEXT 48H lines included; drop \"(Q70, Q90)\"-style references). Its QUESTIONS line becomes one plain sentence of at most about 300 characters, e.g. \"Questions: four settled today, all called right; a 9 Dec Fed hike is now 94% likely; KOSPI falling below 4,600 by 4 Dec looks much less likely; full table at the bottom.\"\n\n3. THEMES: in each theme, straight after its \"My read & lean\", one line \"Questions here:\" giving each open question that bears on the theme in plain words with its probability then and now and why it moved, e.g. \"USDKRW above 1,360 by 4 Dec: 28% to 7% (model), foreigners bought KRW 1.16tn of KOSPI\". The id may follow in brackets, e.g. \"(Q85)\". A question that bears on no theme goes only in the table.\n\n4. OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD. A section with its own <h2> heading exactly \"OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD\", printed after SHADOW BOOK and straight before the FOOTER heading. In order:\n(a) every yellow tag the edition would have printed without this rule (odds moves, two-way tags, resolution tags), moved here word for word with its inline style unchanged (same [n] number, \"Qnn NET <arrow>\" head, question, resolves, Implied, evidence, Echo and Priced segments), one tag per <p>, in the original order. The dashboard parser reads these tags wherever they sit, so their format must not change.\n(b) a <table>, one row per question open after this edition (moved, unmoved and opened today), sorted by resolve date, columns: id · the question in words · resolves · probability at the previous edition → now with its source (market, model or desk; \"n/a (desk)\" when none, \"—\" when unknown, never a guess) · today's move in words (more likely, less likely, two-way, unchanged) · net to date.\n(c) one line \"Settled today: <question in words> <YES or NO>, our call <HIT, MISS or FLAT> · ...\" or \"Settled today: none\".\nUse <p>, <span>, <b>, <br> and <table> only, no <div> (R38 point 0).\n\n5. The footer QUESTION LIST block prints exactly as before (the dashboard reads its New, Resolved, Retired and Open lines). Ids and arrows stay as they are in the themes' own text, RADAR, LEDGER, trade cards and the footer.\n\n6. R33: the ODDS BOARD and the themes' \"Questions here\" lines are never trimmed. R38: this rule overrides R38's \"every word stays\" for the READ FIRST box and the 60 seconds.\n\n7. CHECK before sending: a script finds no match of /\\bQ\\d{2,}\\b|[↑↓↔]/ in the text of the READ FIRST box or the 60 SECONDS section, and counts one ODDS BOARD row per open question; on a failure fix and re-check once. FOOTER line: \"Top plain: yes · odds board <n> open\".", "rationale": "The owner reads the 60 seconds first and the bracketed question labels (\"[1 · Q84 NET ↓↓]\") carry no meaning for him there; he asked for the ids to go from that section only, with a list of all open questions and their probability changes at the bottom. The yellow tags are what dash-ingest parses into dash.q_moves, and the parser reads them anywhere in the body, so moving them whole to the new section keeps the dashboard's Questions page intact; tested in the thread on the 28 Nov Fable HTML (identical moves, events and scorecard). The prompts are at their byte cap, so this goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Fable 28 Nov 2026 edition: 10 yellow tags, all inside THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS; extractQuestions and parseDigest on the edited HTML gave the same 6 moves, 13 events and scorecard as the original. Thread 'Drop question ids from 60-second summary'.", "revert_if": "Revert if the dashboard Questions page loses moves on a day the board printed them, or the owner says the board adds nothing.", "review_due": "2026-12-12", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
-- amendment 28 Nov evening, applied as:
-- update dash.rules set title = <title above>, body = <body above> where rid = 'R46';
